{"reason": "The trajectory shows plateau at 0.9998 AUC, indicating near-perfect performance. The frozen ResNet50 backbone leaves significant room for improvement by fine-tuning. A Tier 3 change to full end-to-end training with data augmentation and a better backbone (EfficientNet-B0) can unlock additional signal and push AUC higher.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Replace frozen feature extraction with end-to-end data loading including augmentation (RandomHorizontalFlip, RandomRotation, ColorJitter). WHY: Frozen backbone limits adaptation to aerial cactus patterns; augmentation improves generalization. HOW: Update CactusDataset to accept both train/val modes, apply augmentations only for training, and load images on-the-fly without pre-extraction. Interface: keep same dataset class signature but remove feature caching.", "model_design": "WHAT: Replace ResNet50 backbone with EfficientNet-B0 (timm.create_model) with a custom classification head (GlobalAvgPool + Dropout + Linear). Enable gradients for all layers. WHY: EfficientNet is more parameter-efficient and captures finer details in 256x256 images. HOW: Load pretrained EfficientNet-B0 from timm, remove original classifier, add nn.Sequential with adaptive avg pool, nn.Dropout(0.3), nn.Linear(1280, 1).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Train end-to-end with AdamW optimizer, CosineAnnealingLR, and FocalLoss (gamma=2.0, alpha=0.75). Use mixed precision and early stopping. WHY: End-to-end fine-tuning allows backbone to adapt to cactus features, potentially boosting AUC beyond 0.9998. HOW: Implement training loop with DataLoader shuffling, gradient scaling, and validation after each epoch. Save best model by AUC. Load best model for test inference."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The trajectory shows plateau at 0.9998 AUC, indicating near-perfect performance. The frozen ResNet50 backbone leaves significant room for improvement by fine-tuning. A Tier 3 change to full end-to-end training with data augmentation and a better backbone (EfficientNet-B0) can unlock additional signal and push AUC higher.",
